WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.234
Don't rewrite it

00:00:01.046 --> 00:00:01.847
in Rust

00:00:01.986 --> 00:00:03.094
Rewrite the slow

00:00:02.906 --> 00:00:03.873
5%

00:00:04.398 --> 00:00:05.942
fast-anything profiles

00:00:05.754 --> 00:00:06.662
a Python

00:00:06.804 --> 00:00:07.900
Node or Ruby

00:00:07.712 --> 00:00:08.796
app and ranks

00:00:08.608 --> 00:00:09.586
its functions by

00:00:09.398 --> 00:00:10.789
time and how

00:00:10.601 --> 00:00:11.744
portable they are

00:00:12.262 --> 00:00:13.193
It records up

00:00:13.005 --> 00:00:14.219
to 500 real

00:00:14.031 --> 00:00:14.585
calls

00:00:14.679 --> 00:00:15.552
has your coding

00:00:15.363 --> 00:00:16.412
agent port just

00:00:16.224 --> 00:00:17.085
that function to

00:00:16.896 --> 00:00:17.521
Rust

00:00:17.604 --> 00:00:18.924
and replays every

00:00:18.736 --> 00:00:19.832
call to prove

00:00:19.644 --> 00:00:20.846
the results match

00:00:21.374 --> 00:00:22.305
Then it swaps

00:00:22.117 --> 00:00:22.977
the Rust version

00:00:22.789 --> 00:00:23.567
in with one

00:00:23.379 --> 00:00:24.109
command

00:00:24.310 --> 00:00:25.725
fully reversible and

00:00:25.608 --> 00:00:26.774
benchmarks the whole

00:00:26.586 --> 00:00:27.553
app before and

00:00:27.365 --> 00:00:28.036
after

00:00:28.566 --> 00:00:29.580
Full story on

00:00:29.391 --> 00:00:30.287
the dashboard
